---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Terms";
const description =
  "Terms for using the site, the archive data, and the optional bundle.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: title,
  description,
  url: new URL("/terms/", Astro.site).toString(),
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="page section">
    <div class="container-prose">
      <header class="page__header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal — please review</p>
        <h1 class="text-balance">Terms</h1>
        <p class="page__meta">Last updated: 2026-04-15</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="page__lede">
          Short version: the archive is free to browse, copy, and use in
          real work. The optional bundle is pay-what-you-want. Don't do
          anything reprehensible with the site and we won't either.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Using the site</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing colorcombinations.org you agree to these terms.
          If you don't, stop browsing — there is no signup, no account,
          nothing else to do.
        </p>

        <h2>2. The archive content</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Hex color values</strong> are facts and are not
            subject to copyright. Use them anywhere, for anything,
            without attribution.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Traditional Japanese color names</strong> (紅 kurenai,
            藍 ai, and the rest) are part of the cultural commons and
            have been in continuous use for centuries. Nobody owns them.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The underlying dataset</strong> for the 348 Wada
            plates comes from the MIT-licensed community project
            <a href="https://github.com/mattdesl/dictionary-of-colour-combinations" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mattdesl/dictionary-of-colour-combinations</a>.
            Use per MIT.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Editorial descriptions, usage notes, curated
            groupings, blog posts, and the site design</strong> are ©
            The Dictionary of Color Combinations. You may quote them
            in design documents, client presentations, and blog posts
            with attribution. Wholesale republication of the editorial
            corpus is not permitted. A linkback to
            colorcombinations.org is appreciated but not required for
            short quotes.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Exports, the API, and embeds</h2>
        <p>
          The export buttons, the
          <a href="/api/">JSON API</a>, and the
          <code>/embed/[slug]</code> widgets are free to use in any
          project, commercial or personal, without attribution. If you
          build something cool on top of them,
          <a href="mailto:hello@colorcombinations.org">tell me</a> —
          it's the best feedback loop.
        </p>

        <h2>4. The support bundle</h2>
        <p>
          The <a href="/shop/">optional bundle</a> is sold through
          Gumroad as a pay-what-you-want item. The bundle is framed as
          a "support the archive" tip jar, not a product — the data
          inside is already on this site and is already on GitHub for
          free. You are buying convenience and supporting the archive
          staying maintained.
        </p>
        <p>
          Gumroad handles payment, fulfilment, refunds, and receipts.
          Gumroad's own terms and refund policy apply to the
          transaction. If a download link fails or a file is broken,
          email
          <a href="mailto:hello@colorcombinations.org">hello@colorcombinations.org</a>
          and we'll fix it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The bundle files (Figma tokens, Tailwind configs, CSS vars,
          SVG plates, JSON) are MIT-licensed — use in any project,
          commercial or personal, no attribution required.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Affiliate links</h2>
        <p>
          Book recommendations on /about, /shop, and in the palette
          sidebar may link through Bookshop.org (primary) or Amazon
          (fallback) with an affiliate tag. When you buy a book through
          these links, we receive a commission at no extra cost to you.
          Affiliate status is disclosed inline wherever a link is
          shown.
        </p>
        <p>
          Design-tool recommendations (Figma, Framer, Coolors) may also
          include affiliate tags where the tool runs a public program.
          Inclusion is based on editorial merit, not commission rate —
          several recommended tools have no affiliate programme and are
          linked at full price.
        </p>

        <h2>6. No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The archive is provided "as is". Hex values are best-effort
          reconstructions of 1933 pigments; they are not authoritative
          for critical print work. Contrast ratios are calculated per
          WCAG 2.2 formulas but should be verified in your final
          rendering context. Use your judgement.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          Don't scrape the site at rates that burden the host
          (CloudFlare may rate-limit abusers). Don't claim authorship
          of the editorial content. Don't use the site as part of a
          service that rebrands it as your own tool without
          substantial added value. Otherwise, do what you like with it.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If these terms change materially, the "Last updated" date
          changes with them. Check back whenever you want; material
          changes are not retroactive.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Netherlands,
          without regard to conflict-of-laws principles. Disputes are
          resolved through the competent courts of the jurisdiction
          where the operator resides.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:hello@colorcombinations.org">hello@colorcombinations.org</a>.
          Response within a reasonable time, usually a few days.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <p class="page__note">
          <strong>Operator note:</strong> this is a starting template
          reflecting the site's actual commercial structure. Legal review
          by qualified counsel is recommended before launching paid
          rails. Section 9 assumes EU / NL jurisdiction — adjust if
          your legal entity is elsewhere.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }

  .page__header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .page__header .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .page__meta {
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  }

  .page__lede {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1vw + 0.75rem, 1.1875rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink-900);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .page__note {
    background-color: var(--color-paper-100);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent-500);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .prose hr {
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    margin-block: 3rem;
  }
</style>
